Z||000003||Foh Fum||04-30-2000||02:02 PM||||Formula,<P>I wish!  Was beginning to plan the trip when I found I have a wedding to go to on the 20th.  Planned to take my wife and do the Lancaster,  Pennsylvania Dutch Country tour as well.  A lot of great 'home style' restaurants there.  Would have been a nice trip.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Anyway, your trip from Waynesburg couldn't be much simpler.  Take I-70 east to the Pa Turnpike and go east all the way to exit 16 (I-70 cuts off at exit 12-Stay on the Pike).  That's it!  Exit 16 is Carlisle.  You can actually see the fairgrounds from the Pike a mile or so before the exit.<P>Happy Motoring!||||reg||1
